{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1005270-2e-spells-from-popculture","id":1005270,"title":"[2E] Spells from popculture","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-19T00:39:08-08:00","id":1005270,"title":"[2E] Spells from popculture","content":"Topic for various rendition of spells founded in other popculture media to work as Mage 2E spells for characters. Various interpretation from different Arcana allowed.<br /> <br /> So let's start with Harry Potter series - WatchMojo made compilation of 10 most famous spells. Here it is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EMQtimSyBXI\" data-code=\"EMQtimSyBXI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/EMQtimSyBXI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> My types:<br /> 10. <i>Accio </i>\u2013 1E it would be <i>Aportation </i>from Space 2, simply. In 2E it will be variant of <i>Co-Location</i> Space 3 spell. Alternative would be small levitation of items, like reverse <i>Telekinetic Strike</i> Force 3 spell.<br /> <br /> 9. <i>Protego</i> \u2013 Simple <i>Ward</i> spell from Space 2 spell. For better effect you can add <i>Wards and Signs</i> to the mix, from Prime 2.<br /> <br /> 8. <i>Wingardium Leviosa </i>\u2013 Levitation spell. Would work as <i>Control Gravity</i> or <i>Telekinesis</i>, from Forces 2 and 3 respectively.<br /> <br /> 7. <i>Stupefy</i> \u2013 Knockdown spell. Works as <i>Telekinetic Strike</i> from Forces 3 with Knock Down Tilt option.<br /> <br /> 6. <i>Petrificus Totalus</i> \u2013 Immobilization spell. It should be Life Ruling spell, probably with each Potency locking 1 Size being ( needing typically 5 Potency per person ) and with Primary Factor as Duration. Alternative could be <i>Control Gravity </i>from Forces 2, intensifying it so much on target, she cannot move.<br /> <br /> 5. <i>Sectumsempra </i>\u2013 Simply <i>Life Force Assault</i> from Life 4 spell with Aggravated damage version.<br /> <br /> 4. <i>Crucio</i> \u2013 Probably <i>Psychic Assault</i> from Mind 3 with penalty option. It <b>can</b> kill it\u2019s subject if used to long.<br /> <br /> 3. <i>Experillamus </i>- Advanced version of <i>Telekinetic Strike</i>, getting also disarm effect with Knock Down one?<br /> <br /> 2. <i>Expecto Patronum </i>\u2013 Maybe it\u2019s G<i>oetic Summons</i> from Mind 3, cast to summon mage\u2019s Daimon in form of animal?<br /> <br /> 1. <i>Avada Kadavra</i> \u2013 Any Adept level spells that makes Aggravated damage to target?<br /> ( I will edit first post with your ideas later )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T00:51:15-08:00","id":1005272,"title":"","content":"Spells from <b>Doctor Strange</b> Marvel movie of this year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Awakening of Strange by Ancient One \u2013 Prime 3 \u2013 <i>Stealing Fire</i> and forced Astral travel of Doctor<br /> \u2018Light\u2019 mandalas and weapons \u2013 Prime 3 \u2013 <i>Platonic Form</i><br /> ;Astral projections\u2019 \u2013 Mind 4 \u2013 <i>Psychic Projection</i><br /> \u2018Mirror Realm\u2019: Creation \u2013 Space 5 \u2013 <i>Pocket Dimension</i><br /> \u2018Mirror Realm\u2019: Bending and traps creation \u2013 Space 3, Practice of Weaving","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T02:18:49-08:00","id":1005282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1005270-2e-spells-from-popculture#post1005270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Topic for various rendition of spells founded in other popculture media to work as Mage 2E spells for characters. Various interpretation from different Arcana allowed.<br /> <br /> So let's start with Harry Potter series - WatchMojo made compilation of 10 most famous spells. Here it is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EMQtimSyBXI\" data-code=\"EMQtimSyBXI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/EMQtimSyBXI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> My types:<br /> 10. <i>Accio </i>\u2013 1E it would be <i>Aportation </i>from Space 2, simply. In 2E it will be variant of <i>Co-Location</i> Space 3 spell. Alternative would be small levitation of items, like reverse <i>Telekinetic Strike</i> Force 3 spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be inclined to do this as a combined casting of Locate Object (Space 1) and Telekinesis (Forces 3). It doesn't make things appear in your hand - it locates them (even if you have no idea where they are) and then makes them fly to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9. <i>Protego</i> \u2013 Simple <i>Ward</i> spell from Space 2 spell. For better effect you can add <i>Wards and Signs</i> to the mix, from Prime 2.<br /> <br /> 8. <i>Wingardium Leviosa </i>\u2013 Levitation spell. Would work as <i>Control Gravity</i> or <i>Telekinesis</i>, from Forces 2 and 3 respectively. </div> </div> </div>These both look good to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. <i>Stupefy</i> \u2013 Knockdown spell. Works as <i>Telekinetic Strike</i> from Forces 3 with Knock Down Tilt option. </div> </div> </div>Stupefy does more than knock people down, though - it's the <i>stunning</i> spell, it knocks people unconscious. There don't seem to be spell effects that do that, exactly... you could impose the Stunned Tilt, but that just leaves someone woozy and confused, not unconscious. You could do Psychic Assault with the penalty Reach - we've seen that some particularly tough people (e.g. Hagrid) can take Stunning spells without dropping, and when McGonnogal was hit by four at once, it took her quite a while to recover. That seems a bit over-the-top for general use, though; most of the time, people seem to recover from Stupefy without any serious long-term effects, and people throw them around without much worrying that they could accidentally kill someone or cause serious injury.<br /> <br /> I dunno, really. It seems a bit contrary to Mage's design philosophy - a spell that you can just use willy-nilly to solve problems without much risk if you happen to use it wrong. So maybe it's not surprising that the Mage spellcasting engine doesn't let you build it easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. <i>Petrificus Totalus</i> \u2013 Immobilization spell. It should be Life Ruling spell, probably with each Potency locking 1 Size being ( needing typically 5 Potency per person ) and with Primary Factor as Duration. Alternative could be <i>Control Gravity </i>from Forces 2, intensifying it so much on target, she cannot move. </div> </div> </div>I think a simpler way of doing it would be a spell that imposed the Immobilised Tilt. Which already exists, helpfully - Enervation (Death 4) imposes the Immobilised Tilt with 1 level of Reach. Achieving the same effect with Life seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. <i>Sectumsempra </i>\u2013 Simply <i>Life Force Assault</i> from Life 4 spell with Aggravated damage version. </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Well, it's clearly an Agg damage spell... Life works, although Life attack spells seem more oriented towards attacking internal organs and tissue rather than ripping the victim open from outside (more efficient). I would go with Forces, myself - a Lethal version of Telekinetic Strike, upgraded to Agg.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. <i>Crucio</i> \u2013 Probably <i>Psychic Assault</i> from Mind 3 with penalty option. It <b>can</b> kill it\u2019s subject if used to long. </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Are there actually any known cases of people dying from the Cruciatus Curse? The most serious cases that come to mind are Longbottom parents, who didn't die but instead went insane. It's possible, of course, that their torturers made sure to heal them so that they could continue to torture them, but I can't think of any other comparable cases suggesting that it can be fatal.<br /> <br /> Assuming we don't want it to be potentially-lethal, I'd go with a Mind 4 effect imposing the Insensate condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. <i>Experillamus </i>- Advanced version of <i>Telekinetic Strike</i>, getting also disarm effect with Knock Down one? </div> </div> </div>Seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. <i>Expecto Patronum </i>\u2013 Maybe it\u2019s G<i>oetic Summons</i> from Mind 3, cast to summon mage\u2019s Daimon in form of animal? </div> </div> </div>Hmm. This is a tricky one, largely because the Patronus Charm exists as a counter to something that doesn't really exist in Mage... the closest analogue to a Dementor would be a powerful Despair spirit, I think, with a Ban or Bane related to positive emotions. Flavour-wise, it <i>does</i> seem like it should be a Goetic summons of some sort, but I don't think a Daimon is the appropriate subject; the Patronus doesn't offer guidance, after all, just comfort. I'd say it's Goetic Summons that brings forth a manifestation of a happy memory (that happens to look like an animal).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. <i>Avada Kadavra</i> \u2013 Any Adept level spells that makes Aggravated damage to target? </div> </div> </div>IMO, this is clearly an Unmaking Life spell. That's what it does: it makes you stop living. There's no &quot;I took a bad hit but I'm alive&quot;; if you're hit by it, you die, unless you're Harry Potter and can pull shenanigans to redirect it, in which case you are fine.<br /> <br /> I'd also add, to the Harry Potter list: the Imperius Curse is clearly Psychic Domination with the +2 Reach option to allow the caster to force the victim to do anything they want.<br /> <br /> And now, some from the Dresden Files:<br /> <br /> - A lot of Harry's <i>ouevre</i> is pretty clearly simple Forces spells (Forzare is a Telekinetic Strike with the Knockdown upgrade, Fuego is a Lethal-damage spell using fire instead of lightning, etc).<br /> - His tracking spell seems like an upgraded version of Locate Object that can function at sympathetic range (since it's impossible to expand a spell area enough to cover more than a small neighbourhood, and we've seen him track things that were much further away than that).<br /> - Little Chicago is clearly a very complex Sympathy Yantra combining Material and Representational Sympathy, designed to allow him to target anywhere in Chicago. The primary use he makes of it seems to be for a sort of mix between Scrying and Psychic Projection; the SFX seem closer to Psychic Projection, but the practical effects seem closer to Scrying, so I'd go with that.<br /> <br /> - Molly's favourite spell is clearly Invisibility, perhaps combined with Incognito Presence.<br /> - She evidently gets considerable mileage out of Hallucination, as well, and various Tilt-inflicting Mind spells like Terrorise.<br /> - Her One-Woman Rave spell seems like a wide-area application of Forces to impose the Blinded and Deafened Tilts (when used for combat, anyway), so, a combined Control Light and Control Sound with Advanced Area and probably +1 Reach for each Tilt.<br /> <br /> - The entropy curses that have shown up a few times seem best represented as sympathetically-cast Miracle spells, possibly combined with Grave Misfortune to be sure that the effects are lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T05:41:19-08:00","id":1005318,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Petrificalus Totallus like other spells would assume a target of Size 5 or less. Even if it didn't, you don't add Potency to hit targets of a bigger size you adjust Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:40:05-08:00","id":1005811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1005270-2e-spells-from-popculture?p=1005282#post1005282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> - Molly's favourite spell is clearly Invisibility, perhaps combined with Incognito Presence.<br /> - She evidently gets considerable mileage out of Hallucination, as well, and various Tilt-inflicting Mind spells like Terrorise.<br /> - Her One-Woman Rave spell seems like a wide-area application of Forces to impose the Blinded and Deafened Tilts (when used for combat, anyway), so, a combined Control Light and Control Sound with Advanced Area and probably +1 Reach for each Tilt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that (within the context of the novels) dickering around with another's mind is a capital offense, I had assumed her veil and illusion type spells were all forces based.<br /> <br /> From the Nightwatch Novels: The Grey Prayer is a spell to destroy corporeal undead (Vampires being a favorite target). I would assume this is a Death Three spell. The only damage spells listed in the 2e are to damage ghosts or living things, but I would guess it would work on a vampire or zombie at that level as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 11-20-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T11:40:21-08:00","id":1006311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1005270-2e-spells-from-popculture?p=1005811#post1005811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that (within the context of the novels) dickering around with another's mind is a capital offense, I had assumed her veil and illusion type spells were all forces based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the specific Law in question forbids the &quot;forcible violation&quot; of someone's mind. It clearly doesn't forbid <i>all</i> mental magic, as we've seen that e.g. mental communication by both word and image is perfectly fine (somehow I doubt that the Merlin of the White Council would have violated the Laws of Magic in front of several hundred wizards including the Senior Council, even with his life at stake). And <i>Changes</i> indicates that while phantasms (illusions created in the subject's mind) are pretty close to the line, they're not actually <i>over</i> it. The illusions Molly uses <i>generally</i> seem to be more Forces-based (probably because when the goal is to either deceive a large group, or overload someone's senses, or both, it's more efficient), but at one point in <i>Ghost Story</i> there's mention of her using a psychic attack that sounds a lot more like shoving a memory (complete with emotional associations) into someone's head than showing them a picture.<br /> <br /> I also recall (and the Dresden Files wiki seems to agree, although frustratingly it doesn't provide a reference) Harry talking about one approach to veiling being to direct people's attention away from you, and we saw Elaine do it in <i>White Night</i> (&quot;Someone was under a veil. Someone good enough to make it subtle. Hard to tell it was there at all. Not invisible so much as extremely boring and unremarkable&quot;). And, having gone and looked up the Molly-POV story <i>Bombshells</i>, she describes that as one of the elements of her standard veil:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Becoming unseen, though, was a different proposition entirely. A good veil would reduce your visibility to little more than a few flickers in the air, to a few vague shadows where they shouldn\u2019t be, but it did more than that. It created a sense of ordinariness in the air around you, an aura of boring unremarkability that you usually only felt in a job you didn\u2019t like, around three thirty in the afternoon. Once you combined that suggestion with a greatly reduced visible profile, remaining unnoticed was at least as easy as breathing. </div> </div> </div>So I feel pretty comfortable with the theory that Molly mixes some Mind-equivalent elements into her illusionary repertoire along with the Forces-equivalent elements. (Notably, she does <i>not</i> have Prime-equivalent illusions; none of them have physical substance.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T12:08:11-08:00","id":1006320,"title":"","content":"Nightwatch Novels<br /> <br /> <b>Sarcophagus of Ages</b> (Time 2)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Advanced and slightly different version of Veil of Moments spell<br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving (with Time 5 - Making)<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> The caster closes target of the spell in a stasis bubble. Target doesn't need to eat, doesn't age or die. Target is also conscious throughout ages to come. Potency acts as Withstand rating in regard to affecting target from the outside and affecting outside world from inside.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The inside is guarded from sight by rust, moss and sediment of times covering the bubble.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Matter 3:</b> Bubble is surrounded by a capsule/tomb shaped out of whatever was present at the site.<br /> <b>Matter 4:</b> Mage can create rock tomb out off the air itself<br /> <br /> <b>Time 5</b> allows for a use of Reach effect described below:<br /> +3 Reach and closing oneself with a target: If the bubble was made invisible by any of the above effects caster can by sacraficing himself make the spell Lasting and impenetrable by any mundane or supernatural force. Only then the spell is trully complete and can be named &quot;Sarcophagus of Ages&quot;<br /> <br /> There's also a mention of a White Haze variant that can possibly close whole army in it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Blade </b>(Forces 4)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Practice</b>: Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> Mage shoots a blade of presurized air which cuts target dealing lethal damage equal to Potency<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: Additional second blade that adds one lethal damage to the pool, divide it in half rounding up and treat damage as different sources. Can be taken twice (divide by three after adding two lethals) assuming the form of famous &quot;Triple-Blade&quot;<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> Potency 4 + 1 let